syntax:
Unqualified function calls within a function body trigger ADL. Consider:

```c++
namespace A {
  struct X {};
  void foo(X) { /* ... */ }
}

void bar(A::X x) {
  foo(x); // ADL finds A::foo
}
```

In this example, `foo(x)` does not explicitly specify the namespace `A`. ADL helps the compiler find `A::foo` because `x`'s type (`A::X`) is considered.
